# Kernel config fragment: Debian 13 amd64 project-specific overrides.
#
# This file is merged on top of:
#   1. The Debian 13 stock kernel .config (from apt-get source linux).
#   2. configs/hardened-overlay.config (linux-hardened defaults).
#
# Any option set here must have a corresponding entry in configs/POLICY.md.
#
# Project-specific overrides (e.g. enabling a feature this target needs that
# hardened-overlay disabled, or further tightening a Debian default) belong
# here.

# --- Container NAT (Docker / Podman / containerd) ------------------------
# We build a newer upstream kernel (7.0.x) than the Debian source whose
# config fragments we seed from (6.12.x). Between those versions the
# iptables Kconfig was reorganized: Debian's old IP_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE
# symbol (which used to `select` the generic xt MASQUERADE target) was
# removed upstream. With nothing left to select it, olddefconfig leaves
# NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MASQUERADE off even though its dependency (NF_NAT=m)
# is met -- so dockerd aborts at startup, unable to program its bridge
# MASQUERADE rule ("Extension MASQUERADE revision 0 not supported, missing
# kernel module?"). Set the generic xt targets explicitly so they no longer
# hinge on a distro symbol that disappeared upstream.
#
#   NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MASQUERADE  xt_MASQUERADE -- dockerd bridge NAT at start
#   NETFILTER_XT_NAT                xt_nat (SNAT/DNAT) -- `docker run -p`
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_MASQUERADE=m
CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_NAT=m
